00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:07.720
John: Do you have any advice for the heartbroken?

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:13.210
Halston: I think, you know, just surround
yourself with your friends and family, and...

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.210
um..

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:15.960
Just remember that you can love again.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.290
Jaz: I would say use it.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:18.570
John: Oh, that's good too!

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:19.570
Halston: Yeah.

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:21.260
Jaz: Yeah, I say, like, do something with
it.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:24.250
Don't just, like, wait for the pain to go
away, kind of embrace it.

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:26.700
Like, write, or paint, or draw, or sing, or
cry.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:31.150
But I think that the best advice, especially
for an emotion that intense, is to use the

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:34.196
emotion because things like that are rare,
and they feel bad, but they are not necessarily

00:03:34.196 --> 00:03:36.080
bad if you use them.

